Graduate & Professional School Resources Internships Fellowships & Graduate Scholarships Internship & Job Search Websites Outcomes Faculty & Staff Resources About OSL Meet the Student Life Staff Student Resources Health & Wellness Counseling Services Service Opportunities Student Code of Conduct Campus Climate Response Team Student Clubs and Organizations Student Programs Greek Life First Generation Program Leadership Rising Program Parking On Campus Student Resources Buy Books Sell Books Shop EC Gear International Student Services Overview Employment Maintaining Status International Student Forms Travel Guidelines Back Donate Donate Planned Giving Matching Gifts More Ways to Give Back Back Current Students Financial Aid Student Portal Resources Buy Books Sell Books Shop EC Gear Coronavirus Student Report Form Back Back Alumni Student Success Initiative Events Meet the Advancement Team Alumni Leadership Alumni Awards Class Notes Milestones Recommend Eureka Shop EC Gear Back Love is in the Museum January 2022 February 2022 March 2022 April 2022 May/June 2022 July 2022 October 2022 February 2023 March 2023 April 2023 September 2023 May 2024 June 2024 Fall 2024 Winter 2024 December 2024 February 2025 March 2025 April 2025 May 2025 Summer 2025 September 2025 December 2025 February 2026 May 2026 August 2026 Back Staff/Faculty Resources Human Resources Shop EC Gear Back Back Apply Deposit Visit Donate Calendar Info Faculty Home / Student Life / Career Services / Career Services Overview / Alumni Services & Opportunities to Give Back Alumni Services & Opportunities to Give Back Career Services and Alumni Partnerships Stay Connected Connect with alumni, students, faculty, staff and friends of Eureka College through the Eureka College Alumni Group through LinkedIn. Career Mentoring/Volunteer Program Register to be a Career Mentor by filling out the form through this link: Alumni Mentor and/or Volunteer Interest Form or contact the office of Career Services directly at 309-467-6431 or email careerservices@eureka.edu . The purpose of the Career Mentoring Program is to help Eureka College students and alumni connect with professionals with experience in their career field of interest. Students and alumni will be able to search the database by industry, job title, city/state, etc. for mentor contact information and will contact you directly by email should there be a match. Respond with your how you wish to be contacted (phone number and/or email address) and expressing your gratitude for their interest. Some questions that might be asked of you: Where do you work and what do you really do? How did you get this job? How did you get your first job in the field? How did Eureka College prepare you for this type of work? Does it require any specialized education or graduate training? What advice would you give someone looking for this type of job? What would a typical first job in this field be today? Can you suggest someone else with whom I can have an informational conversation? Would it be possible to “shadow” you at work for a day or two, so I can get a sense of day-to-day activities? Alumni Career Services If you graduated from Eureka College and need career services, the office of Career Services is a resource you can use! Any current or former Eureka College students are welcome to utilize Career Services. Contact the office for assistance with career counseling, resume creation and updates, cover letter assistance, career searches, job applications, career changes, and more. We can provide up to date information to help you make informed decisions about your next career move. Contact us for more information or to set up an appointment. Internship or Job Postings If you or your organzation have internship or job postings available for students, please email them directly to David Speiser, Director of Career Services at dspeiser@eureka.edu and thank you in advance for thinking of Eureka College students! Back Give to Eureka College 300 East College Avenue  Eureka, IL 61530-1500 (888) 438-7352 Get In Touch Name Email Address Phone Mailing Address City State Zip Country Type of Student Please Select Prospective Freshman Transfer Re-Enroll Continuing Education Type of Contact Please Select Prospective Student Prospective Parent/Guardian Alumni Donor Friend of College Comments Submit Resources Annual Security Report Student Accounts Campus Map Consumer Information Dickinson Commons Staff Directory EID Statement Employment Marketing Student Handbook Technology Title IX Connect With Us Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Google Hours 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Monday through Friday Copyright © 2025. Eureka College. All Rights Reserved. | Privacy Policy CYBERNAUTIC WEB DESIGN"
    },
