. If you need help adding Eureka College, please refer to this article, School Network Management . If you have additional questions, please contact Career Services at careerservices@eureka.edu . We look forward to partnering with you! Eureka College students have over 25 majors from which to choose to study. They also have over 40 organizations, several athletic teams, and several fraternities to choose to contribute to as members and leaders. Career Services also offers students the opportunity to become involved in internships from their sophomore year in a variety of locations and businesses. We believe that these kinds of opportunities add to the academic experience at Eureka College and make our students the kind of well-rounded, critical-thinking, good team members employers are looking for. Students also participate in a number of job search preparation activities – often sponsored or facilitated by local employers. If you would like to become involved in these activities for our students please contact Career Services at careerservices@eureka.edu . Micro-Internships--a Project-Based Solution Parker Dewey helps employers connect with early-career talent more effectively by providing access to real, professional work experiences that showcase skills, motivation, and fit. It's a low-lift, high-impact way to engage talent and give your team the insights it needs to hire with confidence. Create an Account and hire a Micro-Intern! Back Give to Eureka College 300 East College Avenue  Eureka, IL 61530-1500 (888) 438-7352 Get In Touch Name Email Address Phone Mailing Address City State Zip Country Type of Student Please Select Prospective Freshman Transfer Re-Enroll Continuing Education Type of Contact Please Select Prospective Student Prospective Parent/Guardian Alumni Donor Friend of College Comments Submit Resources Annual Security Report Student Accounts Campus Map Consumer Information Dickinson Commons Staff Directory EID Statement Employment Marketing Student 