nternship searches should be treated like a job search. Oftentimes, they are competitive, and require an interview process. Students can search for internship opportunities on Handshake . Looking to partner with Eureka College for an Internship or Micro-Internship? Visit our Employer Page . Micro-Internships Need to build experience prior to gaining an internship? Check out Micro-Internship opportunities available through Parker Dewey. Through Parker Dewey’s Micro-Internships, you can go beyond your résumé to demonstrate your skills to companies, allowing you to explore career paths and expand your network. These projects allow for flexibility – most projects are completed remotely, typically involve 10-40 hours of work, and are deadline-driven as opposed to set working hours. Set up your profile with your Eureka College email through Parker Dewey and start applying today! Forage Job Simulations Forage is an online resource which offers free virtual experience programs designed by industry-leadings companies such as CITI, Bank of America, Johnson & Johnson, Bloomberg, and more. By making a free account, Eureka College students and alumni can develop their skills and gain real understandings of different roles and industries. These self-paced modules contain similar tasks to those completed via an internship. Activate your free account and start improving your employment prospects! Back Give to Eureka College 300 East College Avenue  Eureka, IL 61530-1500 (888) 438-7352 Get In Touch Name Email Address Phone Mailing Address City State Zip Country Type of Student Please Select Prospective Freshman Transfer Re-Enroll Continuing Education Type of Contact Please Select Prospective Student Prospective Parent/Guardian Alumni Donor Friend of College Comments Submit Resources Annual Security Report Student Accounts Campus Map Consumer Information Dickinson Commons Staff Directory EID Statement Employment Marketing Student Handbook Technology Title IX Connect With Us Facebook 