& Professional School Resources Internships Fellowships & Graduate Scholarships Internship & Job Search Websites Outcomes Faculty & Staff Resources About OSL Meet the Student Life Staff Student Resources Health & Wellness Counseling Services Service Opportunities Student Code of Conduct Campus Climate Response Team Student Clubs and Organizations Student Programs Greek Life First Generation Program Leadership Rising Program Parking On Campus Student Resources Buy Books Sell Books Shop EC Gear International Student Services Overview Employment Maintaining Status International Student Forms Travel Guidelines Back Donate Donate Planned Giving Matching Gifts More Ways to Give Back Back Current Students Financial Aid Student Portal Resources Buy Books Sell Books Shop EC Gear Coronavirus Student Report Form Back Back Alumni Student Success Initiative Events Meet the Advancement Team Alumni Leadership Alumni Awards Class Notes Milestones Recommend Eureka Shop EC Gear Back Love is in the Museum January 2022 February 2022 March 2022 April 2022 May/June 2022 July 2022 October 2022 February 2023 March 2023 April 2023 September 2023 May 2024 June 2024 Fall 2024 Winter 2024 December 2024 February 2025 March 2025 April 2025 May 2025 Summer 2025 September 2025 December 2025 February 2026 May 2026 August 2026 Back Staff/Faculty Resources Human Resources Shop EC Gear Back Back Apply Deposit Visit Donate Calendar Info Faculty Home / Student Life / Career Services / Career Services Overview / Fellowships & Graduate Scholarships Fellowships & Graduate Scholarships Fellowships and Scholarships Fellowship Programs are designed to support a range of experiences and activities, including: graduate study in a specific field, research to advance work on a particular issue, and other opportunities to further explore a particular field of work. They are generally short-term (a few months to several years), sponsored by a specific association or organization seeking to expand leadership in their field, and fellows typically receive a salary or stipend. Fellowships have traditionally been awarded to graduate and post-graduate students, but there are an increasing number of fellowships available to undergraduates and new college graduates. Note: Some have firm application deadlines, and others have rolling application dates. Review the application requirements and plan accordingly. Peace Corps Smithsonian Institution Office of Fellowships and Internships Association of Public Health Laboratories Environmental Health and Emerging Infectious Disease Fellowships ProFellow Fellowships Database : Database of over 700 professional and academic fellowship programs American India Foundation William J. Clinton Fellowship for Service in India Samuel Huntington Public Service Award :  Award for one year of post-bachelor’s public service work U.S. Environmental Protection Agency Fellowships provide fellowships for both undergraduate and graduate research work Herbert Scoville Jr. Peace Fellowship provides recent college and graduate school alumni with a chance to gain a DC perspective on key issues of peace & security The William Jefferson Clinton Scholarships assist undergraduate students wishing to study the Arab world in Dubai Point Foundation:  The National LGBTQ Scholarship Fund offers scholarships specifically for LGBTQ students James Madison Memorial Fellowship Foundation Offers $24,000 James Madison Graduate Fellowships to individuals desiring to become outstanding teachers of the American Constitution at the secondary school level Studio Art Centers International – Florence Scholarships : Undergraduate & graduate art scholarships Donald M. Payne International Development Fellowship Program For those with an interest in foreign affairs, a commitment to pursue a USAID Foreign Service career Echoing Green Fellowship Programs – Provides seed-stage funding to bring about positive social change Coro Fellows Program – check during fall 2016 for application deadlines Fulbright Program – online application deadline is October 11, 2016 Gates Cambridge Global Scholarship – NOTE : short application open and close dates – September 5, 2017 through October 12, 2017 Harry S. Truman Scholarship Foundation – for students entering the public service field.  See website for more information and dates. Marshall Scholarship – for post-graduate study in the United Kingdom.  NOTE: Application deadline is October 3, 2017. Rhodes Scholarship – NOTE:  application deadline is October 5, 2016 at 111:59 pm EST. Omicron Delta Kappa – National Leadership Honor Society – application portal to open in December 2016.  Check the website for information. Post-Graduate Service Year Opportunities A service year is a full-time stipend position for young Americans looking to make an impact on education, the environment, or other community issues they care about. By doing a service year, you can travel to new places, meet new people, learn new skills, and gain valuable experience. The federal government, non-profit organizations, and other public agencies that work to improve lives sponsor service year positions. For serving, corps members often receive living stipends, higher education loan reimbursements, specialized skills training, and other benefits. By serving, you will join a nationwide community of corps members and alums committed to making a difference and supporting each other through their service and beyond. No matter where you are in your education or career, service is a worthwhile investment that will shape your future and community for years to come. Note: Check back often for additional opportunities and application deadline dates. Service Year Corporation for National and Community Service Food Corps The Student Conservation Association City Year Change Corps Teach for America Back Give to Eureka College 300 East College Avenue  Eureka, IL 61530-1500 (888) 438-7352 Get In Touch Name Email Address Phone Mailing Address City State Zip Country T