rces Internships Fellowships & Graduate Scholarships Internship & Job Search Websites Outcomes Faculty & Staff Resources About OSL Meet the Student Life Staff Student Resources Health & Wellness Counseling Services Service Opportunities Student Code of Conduct Campus Climate Response Team Student Clubs and Organizations Student Programs Greek Life First Generation Program Leadership Rising Program Parking On Campus Student Resources Buy Books Sell Books Shop EC Gear International Student Services Overview Employment Maintaining Status International Student Forms Travel Guidelines Back Donate Donate Planned Giving Matching Gifts More Ways to Give Back Back Current Students Financial Aid Student Portal Resources Buy Books Sell Books Shop EC Gear Coronavirus Student Report Form Back Back Alumni Student Success Initiative Events Meet the Advancement Team Alumni Leadership Alumni Awards Class Notes Milestones Recommend Eureka Shop EC Gear Back Love is in the Museum January 2022 February 2022 March 2022 April 2022 May/June 2022 July 2022 October 2022 February 2023 March 2023 April 2023 September 2023 May 2024 June 2024 Fall 2024 Winter 2024 December 2024 February 2025 March 2025 April 2025 May 2025 Summer 2025 September 2025 December 2025 February 2026 May 2026 August 2026 Back Staff/Faculty Resources Human Resources Shop EC Gear Back Back Apply Deposit Visit Donate Calendar Info Faculty Home / Student Life / Career Services / Career Services Overview / Outcomes Outcomes First Destination Study August 2020–December 2020–May 2021 The First Destination Study/Outcomes is prepared annually by the Office of Career Services to summarize the post-graduation outcomes of the graduates and provide some insight as to the initial pathways of graduates who are entering the workforce as professionals or as students continuing their education. This report includes data from undergraduates earning degrees from the graduating classes between July 1, 2020 and June 30, 2021 (August 2020, December 2020 and May 2021). The standards utilized to define the graduation class are consistent with the definition used by the U.S. Department of Education in gathering education statistics for it's IPEDS database. This year's survey continues to follow questions designed and developed by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) standard and protocols. Survey Highlights: Career Services collect information at three points in time: at graduation, 6 months and 12 months. The percentage of graduates for whom we have reasonable and verifiable knowledge of their post-graduation activities (Knowledge Rate) is 92% . The Career Outcomes Rate for Eureka College’s 2017-2018 graduates is 96% . Data shows 100% of graduates felt they were prepared to succeed. 100% of graduates believed their Eureka College education was a good value. Back Give to Eureka College 300 East College Avenue  Eureka, IL 61530-1500 (888) 438-7352 Get In Touch Name Email Address Phone Mailing Address City State Zip Country Type of Student Please Select Prospective Freshman Transfer Re-Enroll Continuing Education Type of Contact Please Select Prospective Student Prospective Parent/Guardian Alumni Donor Friend of College Comments Submit Resources Annual Security Report Student Accounts Campus Map Consumer Information Dickinson Commons Staff Directory EID Statement Employment Marketing Student Handbook Technology Title IX Connect With Us Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Google Hours 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Monday through Friday Copyright © 2025. Eureka College. All Rights Reserved. | Privacy Policy CYBERNAUTIC WEB DESIGN"
