xperience, has the opportunity to indicate if there will be additional requirements that will be evaluated along with the student’s actual performance at the site and how the experience will be supervised. Please see the Intern Requirements and Expectations for a more thorough description of the internship process. U.S. Internships:  A Definition and Criteria to Assess Opportunities and Determine the Implications for Compensation National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) Internships Under the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) Class Presentations: Let Career Services bring career‐related information to your class. Workshops and class presentations or resume writing, cover letters, interviewing, networking, job search strategies, online resources as well as employer and alumni presentations. To schedule, contact the Director of Career Services. Online Resources FERPA Primer: The Basics and Beyond National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) A Faculty Guide to Ethical and Legal Standards in Student Hiring National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) Legal Q&A:  Can career services or faculty prescreen candidates for an employer? National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) Suggested Guidelines for Writing References National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) Back Give to Eureka College 300 East College Avenue  Eureka, IL 61530-1500 (888) 438-7352 Get In Touch Name Email Address Phone Mailing Address City State Zip Country Type of Student Please Select Prospective Freshman Transfer Re-Enroll Continuing Education Type of Contact Please Select Prospective Student Prospective Parent/Guardian Alumni Donor Friend of College Comments Submit Resources Annual Security Report Student Accounts Campus Map Consumer Information Dickinson Commons Staff Directory EID Statement Employment Marketing Student Handbook Technology Title IX Connect With Us Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Google Hours 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Monday thr